"This page gives an overview of the inputs and outputs of the IBM Quantum Estimator primitive, which executes workloads on IBM Quantum&reg; compute resources. Estimator lets you efficiently define vectorized workloads by using a data structure called a [**Primitive Unified Bloc (PUB)**](/guides/primitive-input-output#pubs). They are used as inputs to the [`run()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/estimator-v2#run) method for the Estimator primitive, which executes the defined workload as a job. Then, after the job has completed, the results are returned in a format that is dependent on both the PUBs used as well as the runtime options specified from the primitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
